scripts/codex-queue.mjs is derived from upstream scripts/codex-queue.mjs.
Modifications add windowsHide and an injectable spawn function for tests.
The owning-rollout discovery in scripts/state.mjs follows the approach in
upstream scripts/session.mjs and has been rewritten for this runtime.
The detached execution / idle-boundary / queue / durable-result design is
inspired by the upstream project. Other files are newly written.

This is not an official Windows release of Joel Farthing's project, and is
not endorsed by Joel Farthing or OpenAI. Author names identify provenance,
not endorsement. No original icons, branding assets or user data are included.

The isolated scripts/ipc-native-process-run.mjs probe adapts protocol handling
from leeguooooo/open-cross-session, src/codex-ipc.ts (MIT, copyright 2026
leeguooooo). License included in licenses/open-cross-session-MIT.txt.
Changes: Windows pipe endpoint; current-thread-only inspect/wake modes; bounded
frames and deadlines; custom toolOutput without official namespace impersonation;
no persistent state, stream following, patches, delegation or automatic retries.
Version 0.4.0 adapts this protocol into scripts/desktop-ipc.mjs for opt-in
implicit completion notifications. Added shared in-memory completion batching,
rollout idle checks and no-retry-on-uncertain-acceptance protection.
